From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retroforge <retroforge@invalid>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 08:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(HomeMenu): a recent app's card is rebuilt when its library
 item is replaced

The home screen kept a recent app's card by name. A library that drops a
game and adds it again leaves LibraryManager with a new LibraryItem of
the same name, and the card stayed on the old one, which has no launch
item: its page showed no art, and Play did nothing (HW, KONKR Pocket FIT,
2026-10-22: Hades, whose only launch item at first was Steam's own
desktop shortcut, removed by the RetroForge plugin in favour of its
Steam library's). A card frees itself on removed_from_library, but it
listens only after its art has loaded, and the removal came first.

A card is now reused only while it shows the very item; otherwise the old
one is freed and a new one built.

---
 core/ui/card_ui/home/cardui_home.gd | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed

--- a/core/ui/card_ui/home/cardui_home.gd
+++ b/core/ui/card_ui/home/cardui_home.gd
@@ -284,10 +284,16 @@
 	for item in library_items:
 		var card: Control
 		
-		# Build a card for each library item if one does not exist
-		if item.name in card_nodes and is_instance_valid(card_nodes[item.name]):
-			card = card_nodes[item.name]
+		# Build a card for each library item if one does not exist. Reuse one only while it shows
+		# this very item: a library that drops a game and adds it again makes a new LibraryItem of
+		# the same name, and a card left on the old one has no launch item (no art; Play does
+		# nothing). Its removed_from_library can come before the card listens for it.
+		var old = card_nodes.get(item.name)  # untyped: a freed card may still be listed
+		if is_instance_valid(old) and (old as GameCard).library_item == item:
+			card = old
 		else:
+			if is_instance_valid(old):
+				old.queue_free()
 			card = await _build_card(item) as Control
 			card_nodes[item.name] = card
 			
